correctly placed.\n\n\n\n**Clarifying Color Transfers**\n\nI'm now clarifying how color transfers work when shifts occur, specifically when an initial value *doesn't* align directly above a color imprint from row 0.  I'm tracking the movement of specific values across rows and their resulting colors after shifts. The previous examples helped to identify that these imprints determine the color assignments in shifted positions.\n\n\n**Refining Output Logic**\n\nI've refined my understanding of the output logic. The markers in row 0 determine color replacements in subsequent rows. Column 0 contains shift codes: 2 (right), 3 (left), 0 (no shift). My rule confirms that non-zero elements in a shifted row adopt a color from row 0 if the same column in row 0 is non-zero, otherwise keeping their original color. Finally, I confirm Row 0 and Column 0 are all zero in the output.\n\n\n",
